    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Homeland Security spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security has obligated $58.7B in contracts in FY2026 to date. That total comes from 22,816 awards with an average award size of $2.6M, and obligations are up 107.2% year over year. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Homeland Security buy?",
      "a": "Homeland Security buys a lot of construction and ship work: Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $28.5B, Ship Building and Repairing accounts for $7.7B, and Security Guards and Patrol Services accounts for $3.5B. Other notable categories include Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services at $2.6B and Computer Systems Design Services at $1.8B."
